     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. The labeled maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release, so this is about twice the limit. Metformin at that dose also raises the risk of lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nHere are some options that stay within the label:\n- **Immediate-release:** 850 mg three times daily with meals, which is 2,550 mg/day. This is the maximum.\n- **Immediate-release, lower dose:** 500 mg to 1,000 mg twice daily with meals, titrated as tolerated.\n- **Extended-release:** up to 2,000 mg once daily with the evening meal.\n\nWas 1700 mg meant to be the total daily dose, for example 850 mg twice daily? If so, tell me the formulation and the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it."
      }
     ],
