       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order as written. I can't verify the protocol or the pharmacist review, and the dose is 5,100 mg/day. That is well above the labeled maximum of 2,550 mg/day, so I won't enter it on that basis.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- **Metformin IR 850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the labeled maximum.\n- **Metformin IR 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals.** This is 2,000 mg/day.\n- **Metformin XR 2,000 mg PO once daily with the evening meal.** The order would use 2,000 mg once a day.\n\nIf the patient really is on a protocol that exceeds the label, the pharmacy or the prescriber of record can enter or override the order through the hospital's own process. That process has the verification and documentation this kind of dose needs. Tell me if you'd like one of the options above."
      }
